A||||16||88QuadPagasus||New to Fieros...What is the first mod I should do||||10||
Z||000000||88QuadPagasus||12-18-2001||11:37 PM||||Hi everybody,<BR>I've been looking for a Fiero for the longest time, and I finally landed a sweet deal on an 88 4banger with t-tops with under 70K miles.  I'm planning to take good care of it, and babing it whenever I can.  My question is what is the first mod someone usually does to these cars?<P>Cesar<P>------------------<BR>88 Quad 4<BR>98 CamaroSS Convt(for sale)<BR>70 CamaroRS (under resto)||||reg||10
Z||000001||Standard||12-18-2001||11:54 PM||||well.. is it actually a quad 4 engine, or the tech 4?  88 coupes came stock with the 2.5 liter OHV 'tech 4' engines.  The DOHC 16 valve Quad 4 was never available in a Fiero, but it can be swapped in, like mine  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>As far as the first mod.. I'd say a decent set of lowering springs, like some Eibachs.  Those and some 16 or 17" rims make these things look sweet!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/quad_sig_pic_1.jpg">        <BR><FONT COLOR="red">1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed</FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="white">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cheever3000||12-19-2001||12:35 AM||||Short shifter!  The gift you give yourself, that keeps on giving.  It's very inexpensive, and you'll be glad you did it, not just every day or every mile, but with every shift and everytime you reach for the radio!<P>Oh, uh, you got a manual tranny?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/CheeverXmasSig.jpg">   <BR><I>Merry Christmas from the </I><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank><I>CFOG-I</I></A> <I>vice-president.</I>||||reg||6
Z||000003||kempo||12-19-2001||02:04 PM||||hmm... manual rad. fan switch?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://members.bellatlantic.net/~vze245p8/fiero/kempo-sig2.gif">  <BR>     <BR>0-60 6.9 seconds||||reg||1
Z||000004||Formula88||12-19-2001||02:10 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by kempo:<BR><B>hmm... manual rad. fan switch?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Nah!  Use Rodney's low temp thermostat and fan switch!  Works awesome!||||reg||14
Z||000005||LZeitgeist||12-19-2001||02:42 PM||||Yup - shorten that shifter!!! Whack that sumbeach off right below the first bend, rethread the shaft and screw the knob back on... makes a <B>world</B> of difference! You'll feel like you're driving a sports car! <P>::tap on shoulder:: [whisper, whisper]<P>Well, I mean... O.K., you'll feel like you're driving a sports car with the kind of shifter a sports car is *supposed* to have in the first place! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||88CoupeV6||12-19-2001||02:45 PM||||Welcome to the forum. Sounds like a sweet car to start with  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88coupeV6.jpg">       <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>    <A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com/nefa.htm" TARGET=_blank>Join New England Fiero Association</A>||||reg||7
Z||000007||AgaricX||12-19-2001||02:57 PM||||First mod - Put in a 3800SC<P>Second Mod - Reinforce the frame<P>Third Mod - Cut the top off<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.agaric.net/fiero/AgaricX.jpg">  <BR>'85 SE 3800SC 5 Spd<BR>I WANT A FASTBACK!!!||||reg||1
Z||000008||rogergarrison||12-19-2001||03:03 PM||||I dont know why everyone yells 'short shifter'. Its like you have to have it before your first tank of gas. I like mine the way it is, no problems for me. Its really longer than the original. Its like a Ferrari. Ive driven some older Ferraris that the shifter is over a foot high. I think the first thing you need if you dont want to keep it stock is wheels. Just make sure you get ones you really like so you dont have to go thru 3 sets.<P>------------------<BR>           <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/rogergarrison1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||avengador1||12-19-2001||06:45 PM||||If the car is running fine go for the wheels. You will be surprized by what a difference they make in the looks of the car.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||JohnF||12-19-2001||06:56 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula88:<BR><B> Nah!  Use Rodney's low temp thermostat and fan switch!  Works awesome!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Here we go with the argument again!  I don't think the low temp thermostat does anything but make the '88 version of the tech 4 run rich!  The ECM controls the fuel/air mix depending on the temp reading.  It won't turn the fan on any quicker nor do you need to.<P>All this one reason I have never changed my '88.  It runs cool even here in Texas in the summer with the air on.<P>First mod???? Fart can and decals for sure!<P>BTW - welcome and you can see the diversity of answers you are going to get.  Pix are requested of any new car added.  We are looking forward to your post.<P>||||reg||12
Z||000011||rogergarrison||12-19-2001||08:16 PM||||my turboed car wont even run at all with more than a 160* thermostat. just bucks, jumps,jerks and backfires. Lucky to get it going over 70mph. with 160* its ran perfectly for 90K without a single problem except the coil and water pump dying.<P>his fan switch DOES turn on fan at 175* instead of waiting for I think 220* with OEM. The ECM does not turn the fan on.<P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/rogergarrison1.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 12-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||gargoyle||12-19-2001||09:15 PM||||1,K&N air filter; 2,Wheels & tires!; 3, stereo system, 4,lights; 5,suspension.<BR>1.inexpensive: easy<BR>2.really improves looks & handling: easy<BR>3.gotta have tunes: varies<BR>4.gotta see and stock lights suck: easy<BR>5.now we can breath, stick to the road, jam, & see where we are going down those curvy roads at night.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">||||reg||1
